[color=#FF2FA4][b]EARLY ACCESS NOTICE[/b][/color]

Limelight is currently in Early Access. Nexus Mods browsing and direct downloads are temporarily marked as under construction while application registration is reviewed.
[/quote]

[color=#2EDBF0][size=5][b]ABOUT LIMELIGHT[/b][/size][/color]

Limelight keeps character model mods organised and lets supported assets switch while [i]Dead as Disco[/i] is still running. Point it at the game once, import a mod archive, and manage the rest from one themed desktop application.

The Live Loader installs and configures its managed runtime components automatically. Users do not need to manually copy UE4SS, bridge, or staging files into the game.

[center][color=#FF2FA4]◆[/color][/center]

[color=#2EDBF0][size=5][b]HIGHLIGHTS[/b][/size][/color]

[list]
[*][b]Character library[/b]
Import ZIP archives, drag and drop mods, rename entries, reject duplicates, and remove mods from one library.

[*][b]Normal Live Loader[/b]
Activate a supported character replacement without restarting the game.

[*][b]X19 LLoader[/b]
Rotate through a chosen cast by keyboard or controller, in order or shuffled.

[*][b]Profiles[/b]
Save reusable groups of characters and assign an entire profile to X19 rotation.

[*][b]Asset-aware switching[/b]
Scan each imported Unreal container and refresh the model, materials, textures, portraits, and supported localisation assets it replaces.

[*][b]Safe switching[/b]
Detect game transitions, block unsafe requests, reuse mounted containers, and show a subtle Limelight pulse while X19 changes character.

[*][b]Compatibility checks[/b]
Verify the game build, UE4SS runtime, Lua bridge, and native bridge before enabling live switching.

[*][b]Recovery and reports[/b]
Repair managed loader files and create privacy-conscious diagnostic or private test reports.

[*][b]Windows integration[/b]
Themed dialogs, a themed file explorer, Discord Rich Presence, optional resource monitoring, and a guided first-run tour.
[/list]

