[center][color=#FF2FA4]◆[/color][/center]

[color=#2EDBF0][size=5][b]REQUIREMENTS[/b][/size][/color]

[list]
[*]Windows 10 or Windows 11, 64-bit
[*]A Steam installation of [i]Dead as Disco[/i]
[*]Enough free space for Limelight, managed loader files, imported mods, and temporary staging
[*]The game must be closed while Limelight installs or repairs the Live Loader
[/list]

The Early Access portable package includes the .NET runtime required by Limelight.

[color=#2EDBF0][size=5][b]GETTING STARTED[/b][/size][/color]

[list=1]
[*]Download the latest Early Access ZIP from [url=https://github.com/Henreh1/Limelight/releases]Releases[/url].
[*]Extract the ZIP to a normal folder, then open [b]Limelight.exe[/b].
[*]Choose the folder containing [b]Dead as Disco[/b] when prompted.
[*]Import a supported mod ZIP, or drag it onto the Limelight window.
[*]Open [b]My Mods[/b] and activate the character you want to use.
[*]Select [b]Launch Game[/b], then choose Normal Live Loader, X19 LLoader, or launch without live switching.
[/list]

Limelight keeps its mod library, profiles, settings, reports, and temporary runtime data inside the current Windows account. Uninstalling the application does not silently delete the user's library.

[center][color=#FF2FA4]◆[/color][/center]

[color=#2EDBF0][size=5][b]LIVE LOADER MODES[/b][/size][/color]

[color=#FF2FA4][size=4][b]NORMAL LIVE LOADER[/b][/size][/color]

Use the character library to choose each active mod manually. This is the simplest mode for players who want one character at a time with full switching feedback.

[color=#FF2FA4][size=4][b]X19 LLOADER[/b][/size][/color]

Build a rotation from individual characters or a saved profile, then advance through it with a configurable keyboard or controller button. X19 supports sequential and shuffled rotation, prevents overlapping requests, and limits input handling to [i]Dead as Disco[/i].

[color=#FF2FA4][size=4][b]NO LIVE LOADER[/b][/size][/color]

Launch the game without starting live switching. This reduces startup time and resource use when Limelight's runtime features are not needed.

[center][color=#FF2FA4]◆[/color][/center]

[color=#2EDBF0][size=5][b]MOD COMPATIBILITY[/b][/size][/color]

Limelight is primarily designed for Unreal Engine IoStore character replacements containing matching [b].pak[/b], [b].ucas[/b], and [b].utoc[/b] files. Imported archives are validated before entering the library.

Live switching depends on the contents and structure of each mod. A mod that works after restarting the game may still contain assets that Unreal cannot safely replace at runtime. See the [url=https://henreh1.github.io/LimelightWiki/mod-compatibility.html]compatibility guide[/url] for current details.

[color=#2EDBF0][size=5][b]NEXUS MODS STATUS[/b][/size][/color]

The Nexus catalogue interface, mod detail pages, image carousel, download history, and credential protection have been implemented and privately tested. Public access is paused until Nexus Mods completes Limelight's application registration review.

Limelight does not expose a personal API key in diagnostic reports. Public builds will follow the registered authentication flow required by Nexus Mods.

[center][color=#FF2FA4]◆[/color][/center]

